  "id": "Compound::DB00200 - Gene::4548",
  "verbalization": "Hydroxocobalamin appears to interact with Mtr through a shared pathway involving cobalamin binding. The evidence suggests that Hydroxocobalamin binds to different molecules—Cubn, Mmachc, and Tcn1—each of which participates in cobalamin binding. This indicates that Hydroxocobalamin may influence the cobalamin-binding process, potentially modulating the activity of Mtr, which is known to participate in cobalamin binding. The integration of these pathways implies that Hydroxocobalamin could act as a modulator of cobalamin binding, possibly through a common intermediate step. The observed scores suggest a strong, consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
